From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emily Marx <emilykmarx@alumni.stanford.edu>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:47:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Give the Node Metrics dashboard a fixed uid

Without one, Grafana assigns a random uid each time it provisions the
dashboard (every deploy), which ends up in message labels (Grafana's
/apis/dashboard.grafana.app/.../dashboards/<uid> calls), so labels differ
between runs for no reason. The Prombench dashboard has one (7gmLoNDmz).
---
 .../cluster-infra/grafana_dashboard_dashboards_noparse.yaml      | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/prombench/manifests/cluster-infra/grafana_dashboard_dashboards_noparse.yaml b/prombench/manifests/cluster-infra/grafana_dashboard_dashboards_noparse.yaml
index 8250885..899b0c0 100644
--- a/prombench/manifests/cluster-infra/grafana_dashboard_dashboards_noparse.yaml
+++ b/prombench/manifests/cluster-infra/grafana_dashboard_dashboards_noparse.yaml
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ data:
       "id": null,
       "title": "Node Metrics",
       "description": "Dashboard to view Node metrics",
+      "uid": "paramtrack-node-metrics",
       "tags": [
         "nodes",
         "node-metrics"
-- 
2.34.1

